  "icon": "trade_fishing",
  "summary": "Fishing is a secondary profession. Anglers catch fish from any water with a fishing pole, and fish in pools (schools) for particular fish. Cooking uses most of what they catch.",
  "gather_verb": "Fishing",
  "gather_phrase": "Fishing in it catches",
  "node_word": "pool",
  "nodes_label": "Fishing pools",
  "nodes_intro": "Pools (schools) are spots in the water where one kind of fish, or a mix of catches, can be fished up. Any water can be fished; a pool only changes what comes up.",
  "node_skill_note": "Fishing pools have no skill requirement on their tooltips. In Classic the skill needed to fish a spot depended on the zone, not the pool; Forever's zone fishing levels are not on the tooltip API and have not been collected.",
  "node_locations_note": "Wowhead's tooltip data has no locations for fishing pools, so there is no map yet. The Wowhead object pages may list them, but they could not be read from this environment.",
